# iceland-device 0.28-9: Fedora Workstation services that have nothing to do on the OnePlus Pad 4 (field report
# 14 Oct 2026: all enabled and running on the installed system). This file sorts before Fedora's 80-workstation /
# 90-default presets, so its "disable" wins at the first boot's preset-all and at "systemctl preset". The package
# applies it once per system (%posttrans, marker /var/lib/iceland/.preset-unused-0.28-9) to units that are still
# enabled; a unit the owner enables again afterwards stays enabled. Nothing is masked or removed.
#
# ModemManager: the tablet has no modem (Wi-Fi only; "No modems were found"). Disabling also removes the D-Bus
#   alias dbus-org.freedesktop.ModemManager1.service, so NetworkManager-wwan can no longer D-Bus-start it (the
#   activation file names that alias); masking is not needed.
disable ModemManager.service
# mdmonitor / mdmonitor-takeover / raid-check: Linux software RAID (md); kernel-iceland has no md driver
#   (no /proc/mdstat) and the tablet has one UFS device.
disable mdmonitor.service
disable mdmonitor-takeover.service
disable raid-check.timer
# smartd: SMART monitoring; UFS has no SMART (its health is in the UFS device descriptor: life_time_estimation_a/b).
disable smartd.service
# 0.28-27 (AUDIT-2026-10-18 U1): rsyslog copies every journal line into /var/log/messages (~35 MB a day of extra
#   writes; journald is persistent already and no package requires rsyslog). journalctl has every line. The
#   package presets it once per system (marker /var/lib/iceland/.preset-unused-0.28-27) while still enabled.
disable rsyslog.service
